<title>USA: USDA sees agreement with EU on rice shortly.</title>
<headline>USDA sees agreement with EU on rice shortly.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. Agriculture Department official said Thursday he was optimistic the United States and the European Union would reach agreement shortly on how to administer the EU tariff-rate quota for rice.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope to get that resolved now, this week, or very early in the New Year,&quot; said August Schumacher, Administrator of USDA's Foreign Agriculture Service.</p>
<p>Schumacher, who was participating in a news conference with Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman, said USDA trade adviser Paul Drazek was in Brussels discussing the issue Thursday.</p>
<p>An EU official said Wednesday the EU was close to reaching a rice import duty deal with the U.S.</p>
<p>Schumacher also said the department was &quot;pretty much hoping&quot; that the full tariff-rate quota amount for 1996 would be rolled into 1997.</p>
</text>
